{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --short; rg -n 'func Test.*(Concurrent|Cancel|Canonical|Carried|Carry)' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_concurrent_test.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results_test.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go | tail -12; rg -n 'R2|R4|D1|D2' .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | head -12\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:355:func TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:378:func TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:395:func TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:411:func TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:429:func TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:445:func TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:477:func TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:492:func TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:507:func TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:581:func TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:601:func TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go:652:func TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink(t *testing.T) {\n36:- R2: The base shall be used only when every condition below holds. Otherwise the run shall execute every check and record `carry.used: false` with the first failing condition as `carry.reason`.\n45:- R4: A carried check shall keep the base result's outcome, exit code, duration, limit state, output and evidence class. It shall add `carried_from`, the head the check actually ran at, preserved through chained carries, and `carried_generated_at`. Counts shall add `carried`. Carried failures and errors shall count toward the run outcome exactly like executed ones.\n110:### Decision D1\n113:### Decision D2\n123:- the base conditions of R2, one fixture each;\n179:- R2 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun test:TestCarryRefusesAFilteredBase test:TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy test:TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds test:TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial test:TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory test:TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead test:TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink\n181:- R4 [satisfied] test:TestCarryKeepsTheOriginalHeadAcrossChainedCarries test:TestCarryKeepsACarriedFailureAFailure\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThree high-severity blockers remain:\n\n- **N17 — Missing dependency leaves bypass symlink detection**, [validate_carry.go:125](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2791357838/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:125). With `b/link -> ../a` and `b.dependsOn=[\"b/link/input\"]`, deleting `a/input` makes `Lstat` fail. The guard skips that dependency, and lexical selection misses `b`, carrying its stale pass.\n- **N18 — Dependency case aliases escape invalidation**, [validate_carry.go:128](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2791357838/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:128). On case-insensitive Unix filesystems, `A/input` can identify `a/input`, while symlink resolution preserves the supplied spelling. Dependency comparison remains case-sensitive; the physical alias check covers module directories only. This conclusion follows from source inspection; that filesystem configuration was not exercised locally.\n- **N19 — Duplicate check IDs can turn failure into success**, [validate_carry.go:142](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2791357838/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:142). Validation permits a default check and appended override with the same name. A failing entry followed by a passing entry shares one ID; the map retains only the pass, which carry then copies into both entries. This violates R4.\n\nR5-N15 is fixed. R5-N16 is partial because missing leaves bypass its new guard.\n\nApplied the review workflow and security, backend-Go, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Focused regression tests, focused `go vet`, and focused race tests passed. Full validation commands were started but had not completed; their sealed canonical evidence is cited below. Assessments could not run because the read-only sandbox denied scratch creation. The checkout remains unchanged, and no attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N17\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 125,\n      \"summary\": \"A missing dependency leaf bypasses dependency symlink refusal. With ordinary modules a and b, committed b/link -> ../a, b selfContained with dependsOn=['b/link/input'], and a baseline b check that requires link/input, delete a/input and commit. Lstat(b/link/input) now returns ENOENT and the guard continues without examining its symlink ancestor. Selection sees a/input, which intersects neither b nor b/link/input, and carries b's old pass. This violates R2 and D1. Inspect existing ancestors before accepting an absent dependency, or conservatively refuse carry when its path cannot be proven unaliased. Evidence: validate_carry.go:122-130, validate_scope.go:171-175 and 220-225; a read-only filesystem probe confirmed that a missing leaf beneath a symlink returns ENOENT.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N18\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 128,\n      \"summary\": \"Declared dependency aliases differing only by case are not guarded. On a case-insensitive Unix filesystem, let discovered modules be a and b, with b selfContained and dependsOn=['A/input']; b reads ../A/input. After changing a/input, Lstat(A/input) succeeds and Unix EvalSymlinks preserves the supplied non-symlink spelling, so this comparison accepts it. declaredDependencyHits compares A/input with Git's a/input case-sensitively, and aliasedModule compares only module directories. b therefore retains a stale pass despite declaring the input it reads. Resolve dependency identity consistently with changed paths or conservatively refuse ambiguous aliases. Evidence: validate_carry.go:124-129 and 233-249, validate_scope.go:220-225, and the installed Go toolchain's filepath/symlink.go and symlink_unix.go. The case-insensitive platform scenario was established by source analysis, not a local platform test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N19\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 142,\n      \"summary\": \"The base map silently collapses duplicate effective check IDs. Matrix parsing and validation do not reject duplicate names, including collisions between stack defaults and appended moduleOverrides checks. For an unchanged module b with two required checks named ok, first program false and then program true, the full baseline records fail followed by pass under b/go/ok. planCarry retains only the later pass, and the carry loop copies that pass for both checks, changing a failed baseline into a successful carried run. This violates R4's requirement that carried failures remain failures. Reject duplicate effective IDs or refuse ambiguous bases before carrying. Evidence: validate.go:633-637, 821-835, 1240-1245 and 1264-1273; validate_carry.go:140-155. A read-only map projection reproduced fail/pass becoming pass/pass.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N15\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:171-175 applies dependency intersection to discovered ancestors as well as undiscovered paths, except the selected owner handled transitively. TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents covers parent and discovered-root dependencies. Ran go test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'Test(Carry|ChangedScope|EngineIdentity|ValidateHeadMoving|DeliveryValidationRunReadsTheCarriedHead)' -count=1 in pose-mcp; both packages passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N16\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:122-130 rejects existing dependencies reached through symlinks, and TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink passed in the focused test run. However, lines 125-126 skip the guard entirely when a dependency leaf is missing, leaving a symlink ancestor unchecked. N17 records the remaining stale-carry sequence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Inspected the spec, ADR, complete implementation diff, result reader, manuals, help and scaffold changes. Swept rename and quoted-name handling, root ownership, discovered and deleted nested dependencies, gitlinks and submodule status, symlinks including absent dependency leaves, case aliases, manifest-free moduleOverrides, stack and effective-check changes, duplicate effective IDs, criticality and policy widening, administrative exclusions, engine identity, pinned HEAD and material cleanliness, chained carry origins, cancellation, and guarded atomic canonical publication. Ran focused regression tests, focused vet, focused race tests, artifact-check, context resolution, suggest-review and recurrence-check. Full validation commands were started but remained incomplete locally; sealed canonical results were inspected separately. Assessment scratch creation failed under the read-only sandbox. No repository changes or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N18\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the explicit selfContained and declared-dependency assumptions, engine identity, material cleanliness and lexical path identity. Physical dependency identity is not established for case aliases. The platform-specific result is a source-based conclusion; local case-insensitive execution remains unverified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected carried entries being silent and excluded from dispatch, cancellation accounting, and canonical publication under the governance write guard with authoritative atomic publication. Focused carry, concurrency and canonical-guard race tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Additive JSON fields preserve decoding compatibility, but duplicate IDs violate the promised outcome-preservation contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Dependency lookup errors are treated as permission to omit alias verification rather than uncertainty requiring safe execution. Duplicate effective IDs are also accepted, as detailed in N19.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The result reader preserves carried origin correctly, but an unsound selection can attach current material bindings to a stale carried observation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected bounded check output, preserved failure context, carry fallback reasons, selected-module explanations and per-check origin fields. Focused fallback and carried-failure tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined CLI argument refusals, additive schema-1 fields and delivery decoding. Legacy records retain their reading behavior and are refused only as carry bases when required eligibility fields are absent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A carried run can upgrade a required failure to a pass through duplicate-ID collapse. N17 and N18 independently permit stale observations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 relies on unchanged-input selection to justify binding carried results to current material. Missing-leaf and case aliases invalidate that premise. Whole-matrix and engine comparison address definition changes but do not repair path identity.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records the structural contract for carrying canonical validation results while preserving each check's true observation head. It also documents the matrix/engine comparison and explicit self-containment trade-off.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The manuals and embedded copies describe refusal for declared dependencies reached through symlinks, but runtime bypasses that guarantee for absent leaves.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N17\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The affected run reports successful carry eligibility rather than an actionable fallback reason, hiding the unresolved dependency alias.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N19\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R4 fails for duplicate effective IDs. R2 and D1 also remain unsatisfied for the alias cases in N17 and N18. Existing regression tests passed but do not cover these sequences.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c2f8d17e41b23cd2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the changed implementation, additive result contract, delivery reader, ADR, CLI help and localized/scaffold documentation. They remain within the approved carry-validation scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N18\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Git revision confinement and bounded output remain present, but dependency path identity can cross the lexical evidence boundary and authorize reuse for changed physical inputs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c2f8d17e41b23cd2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the selected coarse module-level reuse with per-check input hashing and manual result merging. Reusing the existing selector with conservative refusal is proportionate and avoids speculative caching machinery. The choice remains valid only when input identity and effective check identity are unambiguous; the blockers require enforcing those conditions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the required command. It reported 15 claims, 20 observations and 985 warning findings, with the trailer-resolved head at index-only commit f835a1bb. The warnings and range difference were not treated as proof of a new implementation defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c2f8d17e41b23cd2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected the sealed structural evidence and ADR directly. A separate local assessment was not run because scratch creation was denied by the read-only sandbox.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:python3 -\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scratch-copy preparation script failed in tempfile.mkdtemp with no usable writable temporary directory. Did not run a persisting assessment in the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used sealed integration evidence and inspected the delivery-reader boundary. Local assessment was not executed because a scratch copy could not be created.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:python3 -\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation failed under the read-only sandbox, so the persisting assessment was not executed in the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion check is deferred until POSE records and verifies the review conclusion. No attestation was recorded by this execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cannot verify this review's attestation before POSE records it; the request explicitly prohibits recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved the backend-Go domain and applied the selected security, documentation-style and backend-Go rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition cites the sealed canonical producer result. Started pose validate --strict independently, but it had not completed locally; no local full-matrix pass is claimed. Inspected the existing canonical record reporting 236 executed and passed checks with material_clean true.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition cites the sealed canonical producer result. Started pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp independently, but it had not completed locally. Focused CLI/pose regression tests, focused vet and focused race tests passed independently.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
